/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/CO2aq.dat -- ONE model species, ONE typed file (the 2026-07-18
  structural decision: the aqueous monolith dismantled; a sealed case copies
  exactly the species it reaches, so the student sees the facts in use).
  Body fields verbatim from the curated catalogue record (citations ride).

  WHY THIS RECORD EXISTS (seam S3 of the electrolyte authoring scope,
  promoted 2026-08-24 on the architect's close-the-seams ruling): the
  open-CO2 authoring path pins CO2aq as an active master, and the catalogue
  shipped only the chemistry record (CO2aq-formation.dat) -- so every case
  had to author this identity locally.  The LLM-authoring benchmark's case D
  hit exactly that hole; this record closes it.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    CO2aq;
formula     "CO2";
charge  0;
MW { value 44.0095; unit g/mol;}
aqueousThermo
{
hfAq { value -413800; unit J/mol;}
sAq  { value 117.6;  unit J/mol/K;}
source "Wagman et al., The NBS Tables of Chemical Thermodynamic Properties, J. Phys. Chem. Ref. Data 11, Suppl. 2 (1982), CO2(aq) -- INTERIM transcription, staged for batch primary review";
reviewStatus interim;
}
